title "Deploy three chained jobs"
trace $CLI bundle deploy

title "Destroy: only one delete fails, yet the summary counts every planned deletion"
# Deletes run children-first (job_03, job_02, job_01); faulting the third makes only
# job_01 fail while job_03 and job_02 are really deleted. logDestroySummary runs from a
# defer, so the summary still prints on the error return (without the defer the error
# would skip it). The count is the planned deletions, not the ones that succeeded, so
# job_01 is reported as deleted although it was not. An accurate partial count is a follow-up.
trace fault.py "POST /api/2.2/jobs/delete" 400 2 1 INVALID_PARAMETER_VALUE
trace musterr $CLI bundle destroy --auto-approve
